y conditions. At the time of analysis, 1 g of each sample was transferred to a crucible and placed in a furnace at 550 °C for 6 h to obtain dry ash of samples. The full digestion of ashes was performed using drops of ­HNO3 (2 N) and then HCl (1 N) solutions. The mixture was heated at 70 °C for 20 min until a light-colored solution was obtained. The residue was washed and filtered into a 50 ml flask using distilled water and Whatman 4 filter paper. Atomic absorption spectrophotometer was used to measure the concentration of different heavy metals in the plant tissues including lead (Pb), cadmium (Cd), chromium (Cr), nickel (Ni), arsenic (As), cobalt (Co), copper (Cu), manganese (Mn) a

