y. The breast milk Cr content in 74.8% of samples were above the safe range recommended by the ­WHO23. An study using a Nigerian population showed that the levels of the Cr in the breast mike was higher than the allowable ­limit28. Postnatal feeding infants through hexavalent Cr-contaminated breast milk can expose them to excessive oxidative ­stress50. Cadmium (Cd) is another toxic element that has unknown function in the human ­body28. The primary sources of Cd exposure in the general population are diet and smoking. It can exert it

